wt clean rm - Back up and remove worktrees

Usage: [1m[36mwt clean rm[0m [36m[OPTIONS][0m [36m[BRANCH]...[0m

[1m[32mArguments:[0m
  [36m[BRANCH]...[0m
          Branches to remove (defaults to current)

[1m[32mOptions:[0m
      [1m[36m--after[0m[36m [0m[36m<DURATION>[0m
          Delay removal, then recheck activity[0m
          
          Return immediately; examples: 10m, 1h, 1d.[0m

      [1m[36m--wait[0m[36m [0m[36m<DURATION>[0m
          Wait in foreground until idle[0m
          
          Wait at most this long, then defer if still busy; examples: 5s, 1m.[0m

      [1m[36m--dry-run[0m
          Preview without changing anything

  [1m[36m-h[0m, [1m[36m--help[0m
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

[1m[32mAutomation:[0m
      [1m[36m--format[0m[36m [0m[36m<FORMAT>[0m
          Output format
          
          [default: text]
          [possible values: text, json]

[1m[32mGlobal Options:[0m
  [1m[36m-C[0m[36m [0m[36m<path>[0m
          Working directory for this command

      [1m[36m--config[0m[36m [0m[36m<path>[0m
          User config file path

      [1m[36m--config-set[0m[36m [0m[36m<toml>[0m
          Override config with inline TOML, e.g. --config-set list.full=true (repeatable)

  [1m[36m-v[0m, [1m[36m--verbose[0m[36m...[0m
          Verbose output (-v: info logs + hook/alias template variables on stderr; -vv: also debug logs and raw subprocess output written to .git/wt/logs/). Set WORKTRUNK_VERBOSE=0|1|2 to apply the same level everywhere — including shell completion, which no flag can reach

  [1m[36m-y[0m, [1m[36m--yes[0m
          Skip approval prompts

Primary and pinned worktrees are refused. A busy worktree is backed up now and marked for removal when nothing runs in it; the calling process counts as busy. To unpin a worktree, run [2mwt clean keep --off[0m for that branch.

[107m [0m [2m[0m[2m[34mwt[0m[2m clean rm feature/auth[0m
[107m [0m [2m[0m[2m[34mwt[0m[2m clean rm feature/auth old-fix [0m[2m[36m--dry-run[0m
[107m [0m [2m[0m[2m[34mwt[0m[2m clean rm feature/auth [0m[2m[36m--after[0m[2m 10m[0m
[107m [0m [2m[0m[2m[34mwt[0m[2m clean rm feature/auth [0m[2m[36m--wait[0m[2m 5s[0m

With [2m--after[0m, the command returns immediately. A detached process waits outside the worktree, then backs up and removes only if the worktree is no longer busy and has not been touched since the request. Otherwise it keeps the worktree and logs the reason. [2m--after[0m and [2m--wait[0m cannot be combined.

With [2m--wait[0m, the command stays in the foreground for up to the given duration until the worktree stops being busy, then backs up and removes it. If it is still busy when the wait ends, normal backup and deferral apply, with exit status 0.

Exit status is 0 when every worktree is removed or deferred, and 1 when any worktree is refused or its backup fails. A deferred worktree is marked for a later [2mwt clean sweep[0m; it is removed once nothing runs in it. There is no continuous cleanup daemon.

